== Usage ==
Because blocks of resin can be broken instantly without any tool, and do not have unusual interactions like [[slime block]], [[honey block]], and [[TNT]], they can be used as a temporary building block that is easy to place and break.<ref>{{tweet|gnembon_mc|1851369514547491006|Finally a good scaffolding/temp block in the game: no side-effects of using/walking/touching it, just a block|October 29, 2024}}</ref>
=== Crafting ingredient ===
{{Crafting usage}}
=== Note blocks ===
Blocks of resin can be placed under [[note block]]s to produce "bass drum" sounds {{in|Java}} or "flute" sounds {{in|Bedrock}}.

=== Sulfur cube ===
{{In development|drop=Chaos Cubed|section=1}}
[[Sulfur cube]]s have the ability to absorb blocks of resin, either through picking them up or being interacted with them. This provides the rubber ball/bouncy effect{{only|bedrock|short=1}} or the golf ball/fast flat {{only|java|short=1}} to the mob when hitting it.

